  nonce: 61b4  # 61b4
  message: "ONE FAMILY MEMBER RETIRED BY WIRING IT, not by deleting it (PR #213). _extract_callee_language had zero production callers and a docstring asserting it is \"used by sink/source matching to filter cross-language pollution\" - a textbook member of this class. It is now a real consumer: _match_propagation_entry takes the language whose catalogue built the index and refuses a foreign callee, which is exactly what the docstring described. A test asserts the matcher references it, so the prose claim now has the executable trigger R16 requires. NOTE FOR THIS GATE DESIGN: this member was found by inspection, not by any gate, and it had been sitting at 100% coverage with its own passing unit test - which is precisely the reachability pattern this item exists to catch. Its measured effect is ZERO flows on the 9-repo cohort (208 cross-language taint call edges, none matching a wrong-language sink), so a gate keyed on behaviour change would not have flagged it either; only reachability would."  # 61b4
